### Patent-Style Description

A portable tactile information presentation apparatus for assisting a visually impaired user comprises a compact main body configured to be worn on, or supported by, an index finger of the user. The main body includes a touch-sensitive panel and an electro-sensitive stimulation panel integrally arranged to define a display surface. The touch-sensitive panel detects contact and movement of the user’s thumb, while the electro-sensitive stimulation panel selectively generates localized tactile or electrocutaneous stimuli corresponding to characters, symbols, patterns, or textures, thereby enabling the user to perceive displayed information through the thumb.

The apparatus further comprises a ring-shaped mounting member configured to receive the index finger and position the display surface within reach of the thumb of the same hand. A near-field communication (NFC) module is disposed within the main body and configured to receive guide information from an external NFC-enabled device or tag. A controller converts the received guide information into stimulation-control signals and drives the electro-sensitive stimulation panel to present the guide information as haptic-texture characters or patterns readable by the user.

### Exemplary Independent Claim

1. **A wearable tactile information presentation apparatus comprising:**  
   a compact main body;  
   a ring-shaped mounting member coupled to the main body and configured to be worn on an index finger of a user;  
   a touch-sensitive panel disposed on the main body and positioned to receive contact from a thumb of the user;  
   an electro-sensitive stimulation panel integrated with the touch-sensitive panel and configured to selectively generate tactile or electrocutaneous output defining one or more haptic-texture characters;  
   a near-field communication receiver configured to receive guide information from an external device or tag; and  
   a controller configured to convert the received guide information into stimulation-control signals and control the electro-sensitive stimulation panel according to the stimulation-control signals, such that the guide information is perceptible by movement or placement of the user’s thumb over the integrated panels.
